# house
## The haven, built out
$ do chart("neworleans.haven")
?if coven_size() > 0 and b4.circle != "stay"
  It is a different thing, now, to come in by the gate. There is a light at the back of the house, and a smell of something being cooked that is not for any of you, which is for the cook, who is a human woman and has been told to ask no questions and has, with great firmness, not asked. There is a murmur of voices upstairs, low and unhurried, the sound of people who are living in a place and not merely hiding in it.
  They gather in the long room, when you come, without being called, as a family does.
  ?if in_circle("prisca") and member("prisca", "status") == "active"
    Prisca has a ledger.
  ?end
  ?if in_circle("fiammetta") and member("fiammetta", "status") == "active"
    Fiammetta has a small blade, and a lemon, and is peeling it.
  ?end
  ?if in_circle("thibault") and member("thibault", "status") == "active"
    Thibault has the day book open on his knee, and is pretending that he has not been listening at the door.
  ?end
  ?if in_circle("hanno") and member("hanno", "status") == "active"
    Hanno, in the corner, has a column of figures that goes the whole way down a page.
  ?end
  ?if _lead != ""
    {name(_lead)} has the floor, as someone does who has been running the family's business for sixty years, and gives the report of the city before anyone has asked: who sits in the Exchange, which of the Valère's neighbors can be trusted with a secret and which with a debt, and which doors in the Tremé open from the inside.
  ?end
  They have all, it appears, been waiting for the one subject, and they come to it with the greatest tact and some hurry. Beaumont has had them watched since Tuesday, and the watchers have been watched, and they have a good deal to say.
  ?if b4.circle == "ahead"
    You say that you are glad they came. It is a very short speech, and it is received with a great deal of attention.
    ?if in_circle("fiammetta") and member("fiammetta", "status") == "active"
      Fiammetta stops peeling. After a moment, without looking up, she says that it is a good deal better than the hill, and goes back to the lemon, and her ears are red.
    ?end
  ?end
  There is a good deal of work to be done in a house that is going to be lived in, and there is, you find, a good deal of money to be spent on it. It is the sort of work that a family is made of.
?elif coven_size() > 0
  The house is very quiet. The others are a long way off, in a country that you have left, and you find that you have sent them, in your head, three letters that you have not written. It is a good house, and it has room in it, and it is waiting.
?else
  The house is very quiet. It is a good house, and there is nobody in it, and the quiet has a quality that you have lived with before and that you are, you find, a little tired of. A man alone can have a haven. It takes a good many more than one to have a home.
?end
:the_works
* Build a training room in the cellar and the long gallery, for the young ones ?if coven_path() and can_acquire("training_hall")
  $ do acquire("training_hall")
  $ standing += 1
  You have a carpenter, and a free mason from the Tremé who is a great deal better than either, and in three nights there is a long, bare, well lit room under the house with a floor of sprung cypress and a wall of mirrors that nobody will be able to look into. It smells of chalk and lamp oil. Fiammetta is in it before the paint is dry. She says that it is exactly like the hill, and that she has not been so happy since, and asks if it may have a rack of foils.
* Set up a blood supply in the Marigny, with a midwife and an apothecary ?if can_acquire("blood_network")
  $ do acquire("blood_network")
  $ secrecy += 1
  $ humanity += 1
  It is done through a woman who delivers children in four parishes and a druggist on the Rue Dauphine who is in her debt, and it is done very carefully, with a receipt book and a rota and a good deal of kindness. Nobody is hurt. A very small sum goes out each week. It is not, you think, a thing that would be anybody's choice of a life. It is a great deal better than the alleys.
* Put a front over the carriage house, a cooperage with a sign ?if can_acquire("front_business")
  $ do acquire("front_business")
  $ secrecy += 1
  $ cunning_brutal += 1
  It sells barrels, and does it well, to the sugar houses. There is a foreman, a very honest German, who is told that the owner is a gentleman of retired habits and bad lungs and will not be seen by day, and who accepts it with the calm of a man from a country where a good many owners are like that. The barrels are, you gather, very good barrels. It is odd to have made a thing that is entirely honest.
* Set Prisca to watch the river house ?if in_circle("prisca") and b4.circle != "stay" and member("prisca", "status") == "active" and task("prisca") != "watch"
  $ do coven_task("prisca", "watch")
  Prisca says that she has already begun, and she says it so exactly that you do not doubt it. She is, she says, going to need an ear in the Beaumont kitchen, and a boy at the Bayou Road toll, and a little money. It is evidently the best news she has had in a century.
* Set Hanno to the books of the coven and the firm ?if in_circle("hanno") and b4.circle != "stay" and member("hanno", "status") == "active" and task("hanno") != "business"
  $ do coven_task("hanno", "business")
  Hanno takes it in the way that a man takes a gift of a good tool, with a nod and no thanks. By the second night he has found a clerk at the bank who has been cooking an account, and has declined, with a certain refinement, to do anything about it that would be of use to the clerk.
* Ask {name(_lead)} to make the introductions the city will need [once] ?if _lead != "" and b4.circle != "stay"
  $ b4.lead_intro = "done"
  $ standing += 1
  $ do discover("the_river_covens")
  {name(_lead)} takes a clean sheet and writes four names on it without stopping. A physician of the Tremé who has been the free people's doctor for twenty years and answers every letter. A printer on Chartres Street who knows what the planters say when they think the press is off. The head clerk of the Exchange, who can be had for a good lunch and a better rumor. And the widow of a pilot, on the Bayou, who has taken in people that the river houses want back. "Not in that order of danger," {name(_lead)} says. "And in the order that I would see them, if I were you."
* Learn what the family can do, and what it will be asked to do [once] ?if coven_size() > 0 and b4.circle != "stay"
  ~> gifts_night
* That will do for tonight
  -> :house_done
-> :the_works
